    "media:imagetext": "*MOUNT COOK AIRLINE\nIS-748\nFLIGHTSAFETY\nINFORMATION\nPlease give your full attention to the safety procedures\nexplained by your cabin crew before your flight. We ask that you\nread this page and the separate Safety Instruction Card located in\nyour seat pocket.\nUNFASTEN\nTIGHTEN\nIMPORTANT. PLEASE READ\n1. Seat belts must be securely fastened for\ntake-off and landing, and when the \"Fasten Seat\nBelt\" sign is on. Experienced travellers wear\ntheir seat belts at all times.\n4. Please keep cabin bags under the\nseat.\n2. Seat trays must be stowed away during\ntake-off and landing.\n2.\n5. Do not use radios television or\ntransparent cigarette lighters in flight.\ndetest Fan\n3. Smoking is permitted only in designated\n'Smoking' zones.\nSmoking is not permitted in\naisles, toilets or 'Non-smoking' zones.\nCigarettes must be extinguished as soon as the\n'No Smoking' sign appears. In fairness to other\npassengers, pipes and cigars are not permitted.\n3.\nO. When the aircraft has landed, please\nremain seated until the aircraft has come to a\ncomplete stop.\n6.\nEMERGENCY PROCEDURES\nBRACE POSITION.\nYou will be requested to adopt this position\nshould an emergency landing be required.\nPlease study the diagram on your SAFETY\nINSTRUCTION CARD.\n$‡#*\n02051*21-002*1\nFalo\nLIFE JACKETS.\nYour SAFETY INSTRUCTION CARD carries\nfitting instructions for lifejackets.\nEMERGENCY EXITS.\nDoor and emergency exits are clearly located on\nyour SAFETY INSTRUCTION CARD.\nMOUNT COOK\nAIRLINE\nthe friendly way to beautiful places.\nDarby 571",
